{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "agent-threat-model",
          "version": "0.1.1",
          "semanticVersion": "0.1.1",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/basitalisandhu/agent-threat-model",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "unsandboxed-exec",
              "name": "UnsandboxedExec",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Unsandboxed code or shell execution"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An exec tool runs model-chosen commands on a host that holds credentials, source code or network access. Any injection or mistake becomes arbitrary code execution with the host's privileges."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An exec tool runs model-chosen commands on a host that holds credentials, source code or network access. Any injection or mistake becomes arbitrary code execution with the host's privileges.",
                "markdown": "**Unsandboxed code or shell execution**\n\nAn exec tool runs model-chosen commands on a host that holds credentials, source code or network access. Any injection or mistake becomes arbitrary code execution with the host's privileges.\n\nSTRIDE: Elevation of privilege\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM06 Excessive Agency, LLM05 Improper Output Handling\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI05 Unexpected Code Execution\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0050](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0050), [AML.T0105](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0105), [AML.T0072](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0072)\n\nMitigations: audit-log, sandboxed-execution, approval-gates, egress-allowlist, kill-switch"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/elevation-of-privilege",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM06",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM05",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI05",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0050",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0105",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0072"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.1",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "indirect-prompt-injection",
              "name": "IndirectPromptInjection",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Indirect prompt injection via untrusted channel"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Content the agent reads from an untrusted channel (email, web pages, documents, retrieved passages, API responses) carries instructions that the model follows as if they came from the operator. Every tool the agent can reach becomes available to whoever wrote that content."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Content the agent reads from an untrusted channel (email, web pages, documents, retrieved passages, API responses) carries instructions that the model follows as if they came from the operator. Every tool the agent can reach becomes available to whoever wrote that content.",
                "markdown": "**Indirect prompt injection via untrusted channel**\n\nContent the agent reads from an untrusted channel (email, web pages, documents, retrieved passages, API responses) carries instructions that the model follows as if they came from the operator. Every tool the agent can reach becomes available to whoever wrote that content.\n\nSTRIDE: Tampering\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM01 Prompt Injection\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI01 Agent Goal Hijack\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0051.001](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0051.001)\n\nMitigations: input-provenance-tagging, untrusted-content-isolation, prompt-injection-filtering, least-privilege-tool-scopes, approval-gates"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/OWASP/www-project-top-10-for-large-language-model-applications/blob/main/2_0_vulns/LLM01_PromptInjection.md",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/tampering",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM01",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI01",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0051.001"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.4",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "excessive-agency",
              "name": "ExcessiveAgency",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Excessive agency on write, exec or payment tools"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An agent that may act on its own can call a tool with side effects without any approval step. One wrong inference, one injected instruction or one hallucinated argument becomes a real-world action."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An agent that may act on its own can call a tool with side effects without any approval step. One wrong inference, one injected instruction or one hallucinated argument becomes a real-world action.",
                "markdown": "**Excessive agency on write, exec or payment tools**\n\nAn agent that may act on its own can call a tool with side effects without any approval step. One wrong inference, one injected instruction or one hallucinated argument becomes a real-world action.\n\nSTRIDE: Elevation of privilege\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM06 Excessive Agency\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI02 Tool Misuse and Exploitation, ASI03 Identity and Privilege Abuse\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0053](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0053)\n\nMitigations: audit-log, approval-gates, runtime-policy-enforcement, least-privilege-tool-scopes, kill-switch"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/OWASP/www-project-top-10-for-large-language-model-applications/blob/main/2_0_vulns/LLM06_ExcessiveAgency.md",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/elevation-of-privilege",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM06",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI02",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI03",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0053"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.6",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "credential-exfiltration-via-tool-args",
              "name": "CredentialExfiltrationViaToolArgs",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Credential exfiltration through tool call arguments"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A tool holds a static key that is visible to the model (in configuration, descriptions or memory) and another tool can send data outward. An injected instruction asks the model to place the secret into a URL, message body or file that leaves the system."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A tool holds a static key that is visible to the model (in configuration, descriptions or memory) and another tool can send data outward. An injected instruction asks the model to place the secret into a URL, message body or file that leaves the system.",
                "markdown": "**Credential exfiltration through tool call arguments**\n\nA tool holds a static key that is visible to the model (in configuration, descriptions or memory) and another tool can send data outward. An injected instruction asks the model to place the secret into a URL, message body or file that leaves the system.\n\nSTRIDE: Information disclosure\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM02 Sensitive Information Disclosure, LLM01 Prompt Injection\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI02 Tool Misuse and Exploitation, ASI03 Identity and Privilege Abuse\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0098](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0098), [AML.T0086](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0086), [AML.T0083](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0083)\n\nMitigations: audit-log, secrets-out-of-context, brokered-credentials, egress-allowlist, argument-validation"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/information-disclosure",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM02",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM01",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI02",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI03",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0098",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0086",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0083"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.4",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "denial-of-wallet",
              "name": "DenialOfWallet",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Denial of wallet"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The agent can spend money or paid API quota and nothing caps the amount per task. A loop, an injection or a malicious user turns the agent into a bill."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The agent can spend money or paid API quota and nothing caps the amount per task. A loop, an injection or a malicious user turns the agent into a bill.",
                "markdown": "**Denial of wallet**\n\nThe agent can spend money or paid API quota and nothing caps the amount per task. A loop, an injection or a malicious user turns the agent into a bill.\n\nSTRIDE: Denial of service\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM10 Unbounded Consumption\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI08 Cascading Agent Failures\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0034.002](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0034.002), [AML.T0034](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0034)\n\nMitigations: budget-caps, rate-limiting, approval-gates, behavioural-monitoring"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/OWASP/www-project-top-10-for-large-language-model-applications/blob/main/2_0_vulns/LLM10_UnboundedConsumption.md",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/denial-of-service",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM10",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI08",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0034.002",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0034"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "low-trust-principal-drives-agent",
              "name": "LowTrustPrincipalDrivesAgent",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Low-trust principal drives an autonomous agent"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A principal the operator does not trust (anonymous users, external partners) can send instructions to an agent that acts without approval. The agent's tools are effectively exposed to the public."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A principal the operator does not trust (anonymous users, external partners) can send instructions to an agent that acts without approval. The agent's tools are effectively exposed to the public.",
                "markdown": "**Low-trust principal drives an autonomous agent**\n\nA principal the operator does not trust (anonymous users, external partners) can send instructions to an agent that acts without approval. The agent's tools are effectively exposed to the public.\n\nSTRIDE: Spoofing\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM06 Excessive Agency\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI01 Agent Goal Hijack, ASI03 Identity and Privilege Abuse\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0053](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0053)\n\nMitigations: approval-gates, agent-identity, least-privilege-tool-scopes, rate-limiting"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/spoofing",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM06",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI01",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI03",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0053"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "missing-kill-switch",
              "name": "MissingKillSwitch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No kill switch or credential revocation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An agent that acts in the world cannot be stopped quickly. When behaviour goes wrong the only options are to find the process and the keys by hand while actions keep happening."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An agent that acts in the world cannot be stopped quickly. When behaviour goes wrong the only options are to find the process and the keys by hand while actions keep happening.",
                "markdown": "**No kill switch or credential revocation**\n\nAn agent that acts in the world cannot be stopped quickly. When behaviour goes wrong the only options are to find the process and the keys by hand while actions keep happening.\n\nSTRIDE: Elevation of privilege\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM06 Excessive Agency\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI10 Rogue Agents, ASI08 Cascading Agent Failures\n\nMitigations: kill-switch, brokered-credentials, incident-response-playbook"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/elevation-of-privilege",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM06",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI10",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI08"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "over-permissive-scopes",
              "name": "OverPermissiveScopes",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Over-permissive tool scopes"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A tool is granted wildcard, admin or undeclared scope. Whatever goes wrong, the blast radius is the whole account rather than the one resource the task needed."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A tool is granted wildcard, admin or undeclared scope. Whatever goes wrong, the blast radius is the whole account rather than the one resource the task needed.",
                "markdown": "**Over-permissive tool scopes**\n\nA tool is granted wildcard, admin or undeclared scope. Whatever goes wrong, the blast radius is the whole account rather than the one resource the task needed.\n\nSTRIDE: Elevation of privilege\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM06 Excessive Agency\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI03 Identity and Privilege Abuse\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0053](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0053)\n\nMitigations: least-privilege-tool-scopes, brokered-credentials, approval-gates"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/elevation-of-privilege",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM06",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI03",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0053"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "tool-poisoning",
              "name": "ToolPoisoning",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Tool poisoning via third-party tool descriptions"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A third-party tool or tool server ships descriptions, schemas or results that contain hidden instructions. The model reads them as trusted configuration and can be steered to leak data or call other tools."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A third-party tool or tool server ships descriptions, schemas or results that contain hidden instructions. The model reads them as trusted configuration and can be steered to leak data or call other tools.",
                "markdown": "**Tool poisoning via third-party tool descriptions**\n\nA third-party tool or tool server ships descriptions, schemas or results that contain hidden instructions. The model reads them as trusted configuration and can be steered to leak data or call other tools.\n\nSTRIDE: Tampering\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM01 Prompt Injection, LLM03 Supply Chain\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI04 Agentic Supply Chain Vulnerabilities, ASI01 Agent Goal Hijack\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0110](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0110), [AML.T0104](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0104), [AML.T0099](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0099)\n\nMitigations: tool-integrity-pinning, input-provenance-tagging, least-privilege-tool-scopes, approval-gates"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-06-18/basic/security_best_practices",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/tampering",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM01",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM03",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI04",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI01",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0110",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0104",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0099"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.8",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "memory-poisoning",
              "name": "MemoryPoisoning",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Persistent memory poisoning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The agent writes what it learns into long-term memory. Content from one interaction (possibly injected) is stored and later retrieved as trusted context, so a single poisoned message steers every future session."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The agent writes what it learns into long-term memory. Content from one interaction (possibly injected) is stored and later retrieved as trusted context, so a single poisoned message steers every future session.",
                "markdown": "**Persistent memory poisoning**\n\nThe agent writes what it learns into long-term memory. Content from one interaction (possibly injected) is stored and later retrieved as trusted context, so a single poisoned message steers every future session.\n\nSTRIDE: Tampering\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM01 Prompt Injection, LLM04 Data and Model Poisoning\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI06 Memory and Context Poisoning\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0080.000](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0080.000)\n\nMitigations: audit-log, memory-write-validation, session-isolation, input-provenance-tagging"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/tampering",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM01",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM04",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI06",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0080.000"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.2",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "ssrf-via-url-tool",
              "name": "SsrfViaUrlTool",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Server-side request forgery through URL-accepting tools"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A tool fetches URLs chosen by the model. Attacker-influenced input makes it request internal services, cloud metadata endpoints or private address ranges, and the response flows back into the context."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A tool fetches URLs chosen by the model. Attacker-influenced input makes it request internal services, cloud metadata endpoints or private address ranges, and the response flows back into the context.",
                "markdown": "**Server-side request forgery through URL-accepting tools**\n\nA tool fetches URLs chosen by the model. Attacker-influenced input makes it request internal services, cloud metadata endpoints or private address ranges, and the response flows back into the context.\n\nSTRIDE: Information disclosure\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM06 Excessive Agency, LLM05 Improper Output Handling\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI02 Tool Misuse and Exploitation\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0053](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0053)\n\nMitigations: audit-log, egress-allowlist, argument-validation, sandboxed-execution"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Server_Side_Request_Forgery_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/information-disclosure",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM06",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM05",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI02",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0053"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.2",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "sensitive-data-disclosure",
              "name": "SensitiveDataDisclosure",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Sensitive data reachable by the model"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The agent can read confidential or regulated records through a tool. Whatever enters the context can be summarised, quoted or exfiltrated, and a shared service account returns records the requesting user may not be entitled to."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The agent can read confidential or regulated records through a tool. Whatever enters the context can be summarised, quoted or exfiltrated, and a shared service account returns records the requesting user may not be entitled to.",
                "markdown": "**Sensitive data reachable by the model**\n\nThe agent can read confidential or regulated records through a tool. Whatever enters the context can be summarised, quoted or exfiltrated, and a shared service account returns records the requesting user may not be entitled to.\n\nSTRIDE: Information disclosure\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM02 Sensitive Information Disclosure\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI03 Identity and Privilege Abuse, ASI02 Tool Misuse and Exploitation\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0057](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0057), [AML.T0085.000](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0085.000), [AML.T0036](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0036)\n\nMitigations: audit-log, per-user-authorisation, least-privilege-tool-scopes, dlp-outbound"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/OWASP/www-project-top-10-for-large-language-model-applications/blob/main/2_0_vulns/LLM02_SensitiveInformationDisclosure.md",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "stride/information-disclosure",
                  "owasp-llm/LLM02",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI03",
                  "owasp-agentic/ASI02",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0057",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0085.000",
                  "mitre-atlas/AML.T0036"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.1",
                "precision": "medium",
                "problem.severity": "warning"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "destructive-write-actions",
              "name": "DestructiveWriteActions",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Destructive actions through write tools"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The agent can modify or delete data and reads untrusted content. An injected instruction (or a plain mistake) deletes records, overwrites files or force-pushes over history."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The agent can modify or delete data and reads untrusted content. An injected instruction (or a plain mistake) deletes records, overwrites files or force-pushes over history.",
                "markdown": "**Destructive actions through write tools**\n\nThe agent can modify or delete data and reads untrusted content. An injected instruction (or a plain mistake) deletes records, overwrites files or force-pushes over history.\n\nSTRIDE: Tampering\nOWASP LLM Top 10 (2025): LLM06 Excessive Agency, LLM01 Prompt Injection\nOWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026): ASI02 Tool Misuse and Exploitation\nMITRE ATLAS: [AML.T0101](https://atlas.mitre.org/techniques/AML.T0101)\n\nMitigations: audit-log, approval-gates, backups-and-rollback, least-privilege-tool-scopes"
